⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Manual Scavenging
node JTI · JTI · ⟦Manual Scavenging:JTI:2ddd76⟧

WHO   — Manual Scavenging — the reality, today · named plainly
WHAT  — The living wound: ~77% of manual scavengers are Dalit; the work is banned (2013 Act) yet persists, with people still dying in sewers and septic tanks. The clearest evidence that caste is a present material reality, not a museum doctrine.
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because honesty requires naming the harm at its sharpest — not as metaphor, but as the work real people are still assigned by birth.
HOW   — By hereditary caste assignment of 'polluting' labor, enforced by poverty and social closure despite the ban.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the doctrine's purity logic, made flesh and excrement — banned on paper, breathing in the sewer; if you want to know if caste is 'gone,' ask who cleans it.

